T01 analysis — every number below is computed from the shipped evidence
root: C:\Users\manur\Repos\wm-research\AA\tests\T01
  evidence/headline: sleeve 'gold_cash', 480 strategy rows, 147952 null rows, 8 bh rows; cost levels 0 bps / 20.8 bps; purpose: T01 engine run: does a smallcase's own index momentum (percentile of its own 65-day range and the sweep of 28 rules on the parent's own index path) time a move of the book's weight into a GOLDBEES/LBES sleeve better than circularly shifted exits with the same exposure? Headline sleeve: 50/50 GOLDBEES/LBES of the non-equity part.
  evidence/cash_sleeve: sleeve 'cash', 480 strategy rows, 147952 null rows, 8 bh rows; cost levels 0 bps / 20.8 bps; purpose: T01 engine run: does a smallcase's own index momentum (percentile of its own 65-day range and the sweep of 28 rules on the parent's own index path) time a move of the book's weight into a GOLDBEES/LBES sleeve better than circularly shifted exits with the same exposure? Robustness R4: 100% LBES sleeve of the non-equity part.

Analysis interpretations (choices this script makes where §2 leaves room):
  A1. Percentile = (draws worse + 0.5 x draws equal) / draws x 100 (§2). 'Equal' is |draw - strategy| <= 1e-12 x max(1, |strategy|), not bit equality: a draw and the strategy that are both fully invested through the same equity fall have the same drawdown in exact arithmetic but differ by float noise, and bit equality would put such draws on either side at random. The percentile under bit equality is computed too, and the script prints how many realisations it would move and by how much.
  A2. null_sd = sample SD (ddof = 1) of after-cost CAGR across the realisation's draws; MDE = 2.8 x null_sd (§3 step 11).
  A3. A book whose config-book-window is NOT REPORTABLE (fewer than 4 switches, or share of decision sessions in the sleeve < 0.05 or > 0.95) cannot count towards a percentile criterion (C1, R4, R5, R6, R7-C1): its percentile may not be quoted, so it is counted as not meeting the threshold; the denominator stays 4. The count ignoring reportability is printed beside it. C2, C3 and R7-C2 compare with B&H, not with the null, so the reportability gate does not apply to them.
  A4. Reportability is judged per row (config x book x window x cost x sleeve) from that row's own n_switches and share_sleeve_weeks; these are cost- and sleeve-independent by construction, and the script prints whether they actually are.
  A5. C2: (strategy max_dd - B&H max_dd) x 100 >= 5.0, both negative fractions, after cost. C3: strategy Calmar > B&H Calmar, strictly. B&H is the 'bh' row (no cost).
  A6. R6 passes only if each of the four neighbours separately reaches percentile >= 75 in >= 3 of 4 books in W1 and in W2. Each neighbour's own verdict is printed too.
  A7. R7 applies C1 and C2 exactly as written to pct_w65_q25_daily (headline run, after cost).
  A8. Multiplicity: the daily config is rotated in sessions, so its offsets k do not align with the weekly configs' offsets (k weeks). It is EXCLUDED from both the best row and the null of best rows; the best row is the best of the 27 weekly-rotated sweep configs, ranked against max-over-27-configs after-cost CAGR at each offset k present for all 27. The daily config's own CAGR and percentile are printed beside it, flagged when it beats the weekly best. T01.md says 'all 28 configs shifted by the same k', which cannot be applied as written (the daily config's k is in sessions and its null has no draw below k = 40), so the literal version is printed beside as a sensitivity: the best of all 28 against the max of all 28 at the same numeric k, over the offsets where all 28 have a draw.
  A9. V1 is read from verify_headline.json and verify_cash_sleeve.json (verify_own_momentum.py's report): mode 'verify', verdict PASS, every check passed having compared rows, and total failures, missing rows and extra rows all 0; plus the verifier's --corrupt-test report verify_<run>_corrupt.json (else any verify_*_corrupt.json: one corrupted-copy test checks the checker, whichever run it copied): corrupted-copy verdict FAIL and every planted defect detected. Without a corrupted-copy report V1 is FAIL (unconfirmed), as the gate requires it. A report written under one of the verifier's diagnostic switches (diagnostic_reading_not_predeclared not False) cannot pass V1; the readings the verifier used, and any reading it changed after the evidence existed, are printed. Whether null rows were checked (not required by V1) is printed. A report in any other shape is read generically: a pass flag or exit code 0, rows compared > 0, failures 0.
  A10. V3 also requires the null grid to be complete: every k with k_min <= k <= n+1-k_min must be present (n+1 = the realisation's decision count in decisions_all_configs.csv), because the gate is stated for every draw.
  A11. Target-level multisets are compared as parsed JSON (levels rounded to 4 decimals, zero counts dropped), not as raw strings, so key order cannot fail a draw.
  A12. Per-year returns: NAV at the year's last session / NAV at the previous year's last session (the first year from T0) - 1, from daily_reference.csv; first and last years are partial and printed with their dates.

Engine interpretations (audit.json, headline):
  E1. Reference config R 'pct_w65_q25_weekly' in T01.md is written as config 'pct_w65_q25' (weekly) in every file.
  E2. Sleeve prices: 'gaps carried forward' is read as as-of alignment (level at a session = the latest observation dated on or before it, including observations on non-calendar dates), the repo convention in final_strategy.py / prices.py / why_n100sc100.py. For LBES this differs from reindex(calendar).ffill() on 31 sessions inside the windows (max level difference 0.84 on ~2000, 0.04%). The LBES tail after 2026-08-09 is a plain forward fill (no accrual).
  E3. Calendar = union of the harness dates (non-null rows of the four parent columns) and the published parentIndices.csv dates. Five dates present in nav_curves_daily.csv but absent from parentIndices.csv (2021-11-04, 2022-10-24, 2024-05-18, 2024-11-01, 2025-10-21) are therefore not sessions.
  E4. Weekly decision sessions: the last session of each ISO (year, week) of the whole calendar falling in (T0, end], plus T0. Weekend special sessions (e.g. Sunday muhurat 2016-10-30, Saturday 2020-11-14, 2024-01-20) are sessions and can be a week's last session.
  E5. History requirement read literally: pct needs W previous closes, sma_n needs n previous closes (one more than its mean uses), tsmom_L needs L, ddhigh needs 250 previous closes, st needs >= 6 completed weekly candles, triple needs a Master label <= d. All are met at every decision in both windows (W1 T0 = global session index 262).
  E6. Rotation direction: w'_j = w_{(j-k) mod (n+1)} (numpy.roll(w, k)). The set of k (8..n+1-8; daily 40..n+1-40) is symmetric, so the set of draws does not depend on the direction, only the shift_k label does.
  E7. If a target is decided on the session before the last (possible only for the daily config), it is traded at the last session's close and then everything is liquidated at the same close (both legs pay cost), because T01 only exempts a target decided on the last session itself.
  E8. n_decisions, share_sleeve_weeks, avg_equity_weight, n_spells and target_level_counts are computed over all n+1 decision sessions, T0 and the (untraded) last session included; n_spells is not circular.
  E9. observed_se uses the window's weekly decision sessions as the weekly grid for every config, including pct_w65_q25_daily; the static mix's equity weight is the config's avg_equity_weight; annualised by multiplying the weekly SE by 52 (the SE of an annual arithmetic mean difference).
  E10. Volatility uses the sample SD (ddof = 1) of daily NAV returns.
  E11. data_last_date is the last input date actually used: the decision date for every P-based config; for st_weekly the label of the weekly candle read (= the decision date on every weekly decision, 2021-10-29 at W2's T0 2021-11-01, whose own week is not complete); for triple the latest Master week label used (it reads no P).
  E12. triple / triple_and_pct25 read each Master file's latest week label <= d. On three of our week-end sessions the Master label is a later date (2021-11-03 vs label 2021-11-04, 2024-05-17 vs 2024-05-18, 2024-10-31 vs 2024-11-01), so those decisions read the previous week's SIGN (point-in-time safe, one week stale).
  E13. st_weekly: candles run over the whole spliced history from 2014-07-04; the supertrend starts on candle index 5 (the 6th), with the production branch order kept verbatim including its 'pst == pflb and close < fub' sell branch and its st = 0 fallback (the fallback never fired: see engine_self_checks.supertrend_line_zero_count). SELL = line equal to the upper band (FUB).
  E14. B&H realisation rows: config 'bh', cost 0, n_decisions = weekly decision count, share_sleeve_weeks 0, avg_equity_weight 1, n_switches 0, n_spells 0.
  E15. trades.csv: from_equity is empty for the build (the book is all cash) and to_equity is empty for the final liquidation; value_traded_frac = (sum of trims at pre-cost value + sum of cash committed to top-ups) / nav_before (for the liquidation, the gross value sold / nav_before).
  E16. daily_reference.csv: weights are fractions of NAV at the close, after that session's trading; w_cash = LBES plus the cash account, so the three sum to 1 (w_cash = 1 at T0, before the build, and at the last session, after the liquidation).
  E17. The hysteresis state starts as equity at each window's T0 (the state machine is run over that window's decision sessions only).

Engine caveats (audit.json, headline):
  - W1 parents are the harness rebuild (price return, no dividends); B&H is understated by roughly the dividend yield there (T01.md section 3, known contaminants).
  - W2 signals in its first year read simulated (pre-2021-11) closes; every lookback is at most 250 sessions.
  - The 2021-10-29 -> 2021-11-01 splice session has a return of 0 by construction.
  - LBES ends 2026-08-09 and is forward-filled for the last sessions of W2 (cash earns 0 there).
  - The null does not match which weeks the sleeve is held (gold's 2024-26 rally); the cash_sleeve run (R4) removes gold's path.
  - The four books share one market; '3 of 4' is a consistency requirement, not four independent tests.

